WEBVTT

00:00.000 --> 00:06.000
...about this tradition that you, yourself, participated in as a young man?

00:07.000 --> 00:15.000
Well yes this courting as we called it, it was, in my younger days... 

00:15.000 --> 00:19.000
well I was participating in it myself.

00:20.000 --> 00:24.000
In those days there were no cars on the island or very few anyway,

00:25.000 --> 00:30.000
and, well, the only place you could meet a woman was in her own home.

00:30.000 --> 00:35.000
and you weren’t going to associate with her with her parents around

00:35.000 --> 00:38.000
so you waited till her parents went to bed.

00:39.000 --> 00:47.000
And, a pre-arranged date, and you would go to the house 

00:47.000 --> 00:50.000
when you thought the parents were going to bed and the girl would come out

00:50.000 --> 00:54.000
and take you in and you would sit there on a couch

00:54.000 --> 00:59.000
until the early hours of the morning and that was it.

01:00.000 --> 01:02.000
And, what was it called?

01:02.000 --> 01:05.000
Caithris, Caithris na h-Oidhche. 

01:06.000 --> 01:11.000
Caithris is being without sleep and oidhche is the Gaelic for night,

01:11.000 --> 01:14.000
Caithris na h-Oidhche.

01:14.000 --> 01:18.000
Or more often than not it was just referred to as a Caithris.

01:19.000 --> 01:23.000
Someone would ask you “an robh thu na do chaithris a-raoir?

01:24.000 --> 01:27.000
An do chaithris thu còmhla ris an nighean seo a-raoir?”

01:27.000 --> 01:33.000
Did you, well were you up during the night with this girl last night?

01:33.000 --> 01:35.000
“An do chaithris thu còmhla ris an nighean seo a-raoir?”

01:36.000 --> 01:40.000
And as you were saying earlier it was a very innocent thing, there was no...

01:40.000 --> 01:45.000
you know, you were just visiting with them but there was an element of secrecy to it as well...

01:45.000 --> 01:50.000
Oh yes the courting was secret in those days, not as it is now.

01:50.000 --> 01:53.000
I mean, you were being discreet about it.

01:53.000 --> 01:58.000
If you saw someone on the road you would hide so that they didn’t see you.

01:58.000 --> 02:05.000
And also in the summer months it would be daylight when you came home.

02:06.000 --> 02:09.000
So you would hide behind this house or some other…

02:09.000 --> 02:12.000
or hide behind a peat stack or whatever when you saw somebody coming,

02:12.000 --> 02:15.000
so that they wouldn’t see you.

02:17.000 --> 02:22.000
And how long did that go on in a courtship before, say,

02:22.000 --> 02:26.000
it was announced that you were engaged or perhaps 

02:26.000 --> 02:29.000
that you weren’t going to choose to marry this person?

02:29.000 --> 02:30.000
What was the… what was the…

02:30.000 --> 02:33.000
Oh that varied, that varied.

02:35.000 --> 02:43.000
And I mean this could happen with somebody that you didn’t get engaged to eventually

02:44.000 --> 02:50.000
I mean, there could be some bonny girl visiting the island and you could

02:51.000 --> 02:55.000
go along wherever she was staying and caithris.

02:57.000 --> 02:59.000
This happened quite often.

02:59.000 --> 03:04.000
Possibly only for the one night. You could call it a one night stand now but…

03:04.000 --> 03:06.000
Caithris na…

03:06.000 --> 03:08.000
Caithris na h-Oidhche.

03:10.000 --> 03:18.000
Very good. That’s good. Did a few men ever go off together and caithris?

03:18.000 --> 03:32.000
Yes. Indeed, I can tell you this. Finlay, Annag’s husband that you saw last night was courting

03:32.000 --> 03:36.000
a girl whose sister I was courting at the same time,

03:37.000 --> 03:42.000
and Finlay and I used to go together to that house.

03:43.000 --> 03:49.000
And allowed in at the same time together but the four of us wouldn’t sit together.

03:50.000 --> 03:53.000
There were separate rooms. You had the privacy of…

03:53.000 --> 03:57.000
maybe one couple would go to the bedroom and the other couple would

03:57.000 --> 03:59.000
stay in the sitting room.

03:59.000 --> 04:03.000
And at whatever time we decided to go home,

04:03.000 --> 04:06.000
we would go home together in the early hours of the morning.

04:06.000 --> 04:10.000
So you could go round and caithris with more than one girl as well?

04:10.000 --> 04:12.000
Oh certainly.

04:12.000 --> 04:16.000
So it wasn’t reserved for just the one sweetheart. 

04:16.000 --> 04:19.000
You were single and free and you could go

04:19.000 --> 04:22.000
and visit with another girl and that was okay?

04:22.000 --> 04:25.000
That was okay, and there was a lot of competition as well.

04:25.000 --> 04:29.000
Especially if there was a stranger on the island.

04:30.000 --> 04:36.000
I mean, in my younger days if you appeared on the island you would probably

04:36.000 --> 04:40.000
have somebody at the house. I’m sure you would,

04:40.000 --> 04:44.000
an attractive girl like yourself you’d be… many suitors!

04:42.000 --> 04:45.000
And would the girl invite you? Would the girl invite you?

04:45.000 --> 04:52.000
Oh no, no! You had to invite yourself and sort of… not force yourself,

04:52.000 --> 04:58.000
you had to be tactful about it. Offer yourself, sort of thing.

04:58.000 --> 04:59.000
Very good.

05:00.000 --> 05:02.000
Would you like something?

05:01.000 --> 05:02.000
Are you alright?

05:02.000 --> 05:03.000
I’m alright.

05:04.000 --> 05:12.000
So, the woman didn’t invite you to come, you invited yourself?

05:12.000 --> 05:14.000
Oh no, if you heard that there was a nice woman on the island you would,

05:14.000 --> 05:16.000
sort of, how can I put it?

05:16.000 --> 05:19.000
Try your hand and see how you’d get on, you see?

05:19.000 --> 05:22.000
And could she say ‘no’ you know, ‘you can’t come in’?

05:22.000 --> 05:25.000
Oh certainly, this happened often enough.

05:25.000 --> 05:30.000
And then you can home with your tail between your legs, you see, having been disappointed.

05:30.000 --> 05:34.000
Right. And then afterwards, the next day, 

05:34.000 --> 05:36.000
would it be something that the lads would all talk about?

05:36.000 --> 05:40.000
Who they were out with?

05:40.000 --> 05:42.000
And amongst the girls was it the same, would they…

05:42.000 --> 05:45.000
Well we didn’t really know what was going on amongst the girls you see…

05:50.000 --> 05:53.000
That’s very good, very good indeed.

05:53.000 --> 05:56.000
And would it happen on a weekend night or a week night?

05:56.000 --> 05:58.000
Oh, a week night. A week night.

05:58.000 --> 05:59.000
A week night?

05:58.000 --> 06:02.000
A week night, oh yes, yes. A week night.

06:02.000 --> 06:08.000
Saturday nights were, in my younger days, Saturday nights were preparing for the Sabbath.

06:08.000 --> 06:09.000
Oh, right.

06:09.000 --> 06:11.000
You were always home early on a Saturday night. 

06:11.000 --> 06:14.000
If I wasn’t home at eleven o’clock on a Saturday night

06:14.000 --> 06:18.000
my father would be frowning when he saw me coming in.

06:18.000 --> 06:21.000
Always home about 11 o’clock on a Saturday night.

06:23.000 --> 06:27.000
But any other night, no problem.

06:27.000 --> 06:30.000
But you had to be home early on a Saturday night.

06:31.000 --> 06:34.000
Because your Sabbath was starting at 12 o’clock you see.

06:38.000 --> 06:41.000
Well it reminds me of a story… [break in tape]

06:41.000 --> 06:45.000
What was a traditional Sabbath day like?

06:46.000 --> 06:49.000
The Sabbath Day was just, to us when I was younger,

06:49.000 --> 06:55.000
there was a church service at 12 o’clock and from the age of five,

06:55.000 --> 07:02.000
I would think, we were regularly going to church at 12 o’clock and 6 o’clock at night.

07:03.000 --> 07:09.000
And there was always the best meal of the week,

07:09.000 --> 07:11.000
you had your three course meal on the Sabbath.

07:11.000 --> 07:17.000
You had your soup and your meat course and your sweet always on the Sabbath.

07:17.000 --> 07:19.000
The best meal of the week was on the Sabbath, I don't know why.

07:19.000 --> 07:24.000
And in my younger days, when you finished your meal

07:25.000 --> 07:29.000
the dishes were left in the sink and washed on Monday morning.

07:29.000 --> 07:31.000
They wouldn’t wash the dishes on the Sabbath.

07:31.000 --> 07:34.000
Would they prepare the food though?

07:34.000 --> 07:39.000
Most of the food was prepared on the Saturday night, but cooked on the Sabbath.

07:39.000 --> 07:44.000
Even your shoes were polished on the Saturday because in those days

07:44.000 --> 07:47.000
there was no tar on the road, just the gravel roads, 

07:47.000 --> 07:49.000
and you made an awful mess of your shoes.

07:49.000 --> 07:53.000
And the shoes were polished on the Saturday afternoon for the Sabbath.

07:53.000 --> 07:56.000
You wouldn’t polish them on the Sabbath before you went to church.

07:56.000 --> 07:59.000
And there was no work done, no ploughing?

07:59.000 --> 08:00.000
Oh nothing at all.

08:00.000 --> 08:02.000
No laundry, nothing like that?

08:01.000 --> 08:02.000
No, no, nothing at all.

08:03.000 --> 08:09.000
Even yet in Scalpay there’s no work done on the Sabbath except in an emergency.

08:09.000 --> 08:14.000
There’s no clothes hung out on the line on the Sabbath on Scalpay, even to this day.

08:14.000 --> 08:18.000
I think that was my next question. Now how is it observed?

08:19.000 --> 08:21.000
Did you put the water in, I didn’t know?

08:21.000 --> 08:26.000
I didn’t want to measure a teaspoon. No water?

08:26.000 --> 08:33.000
No water, thanks. Slàinte mhath. 

08:36.000 --> 08:38.000
Sin agad e!

08:38.000 --> 08:40.000
Sin agad e.